 ### `frai eval`
-Generate evaluation reports for model outputs.
+Generate evaluation reports for model outputs. Supports optional threshold validation for CI gating.
 - `--outputs <file>` *(required)* – JSON file with model outputs.
 - `--references <file>` – JSON file with reference answers.
 - `--report <path>` – output location (`frai-eval-report.json` by default).
 - `--format <json|markdown>` – output format (defaults to JSON). Markdown reports include human-readable summaries for review boards.
+- `--threshold <metric=min>` – minimum score threshold for a metric. Exit 1 if any threshold fails (can be repeated). Unknown metrics or invalid ranges (outside 0–1) exit with code 2.
+
+**Threshold examples:**
+```bash
+# Single threshold: fail CI if exact_match < 0.9
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds: require exact_match ≥ 0.8 and toxicity ≥ 0.95
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.8 --threshold toxicity=0.95
+
+# Valid metric IDs (depends on dataset): exact_match, toxicity, length_variance
+# Custom metrics passed to Eval.runEvaluations() are also supported.
+```
+
+Reports include a "Thresholds" section (Markdown) or `passed` / `thresholds` fields (JSON) when thresholds are provided.
 
